Crème caramel
4
Crème caramel baked in a bain-marie with homemade caramel.

---
Caramel
water|80|ml
powdered sugar|150|g

Custard
semi-skimmed milk|500|ml
powdered sugar|80|g
eggs|3|pcs
vanilla pod|1|pcs

---
Make the caramel: put the water and sugar in a saucepan and cook until you get an amber caramel.
Pour half of the hot caramel into ramekins and swirl to coat the bottom.
With the rest, optionally make decorations on baking paper and let set.

Preheat the oven to 130°C.
Bring the milk to the boil with the split and scraped vanilla pod.
Whisk the eggs with the sugar, then pour in the hot milk while whisking.
Strain the custard.

Fill the caramelised ramekins with the custard.
Place the ramekins in a large dish and add hot water to halfway up (bain-marie).
Bake about 45 min at 130°C, until the custards are set.
Let cool then refrigerate for at least 1 hour.

To serve, turn out the custards onto the centre of plates.
Coat with the remaining caramel and decorate with caramel pieces.

---
Check doneness: the custard should be set but still slightly wobbly in the centre.
Making a small amount of caramel requires care to avoid burning or crystallising.

---
dessert
